      answer: "**Objection Process:**\n\n**Time Limit:**\n\n• **30 days** from date of service of assessment notice\n• Tax authority may **extend** time for good cause\n\n**What You Need to Include:**\n\nYour objection notice must contain:\n\n• **Specific issues disputed** with monetary values\n• **Amendments required** to resolve the dispute\n• **Justification** for the amendments\n• **Amount admitted** - Your assessable income/profits for the period\n• **Tax admitted** - Amount of tax you admit is payable (or nil)\n\n**Process:**\n\n1. **File written objection** - In person, courier, or electronically\n2. **Tax authority may request** - Additional particulars, books, documents\n3. **Tax authority responds** - Within **90 days** (or your objection is upheld)\n4. **Agreement reached** - Assessment amended, revised notice served\n5. **No agreement** - You can exercise **right of appeal** to Tax Appeal Tribunal\n\n**Important:**\n\n• **Be specific** - General objections may be rejected\n• **Provide evidence** - Support your objection with documents\n• **Respond promptly** - To any requests from tax authority\n• **90-day rule** - If tax authority doesn't respond in 90 days, your objection is upheld\n\n**Appeal:**\n\nIf objection is rejected or not agreed:\n\n• Appeal to **Tax Appeal Tribunal** within 30 days\n• Further appeal to **Federal High Court** (on points of law)\n• Then **Court of Appeal** and **Supreme Court**\n\n**Note:** Keep all records and documentation to support your objection.",
