      question: "What is an Advance Ruling and how can I get one?",
      answer: "**Advance Rulings:**\n\n**What is It?**\n\nAn advance ruling provides **clarity and certainty** on how tax laws apply to your specific transaction or situation.\n\n**Benefits:**\n\n• **Clarity** - Understand tax implications before transacting\n• **Consistency** - Consistent application of tax law\n• **Certainty** - Know your tax position in advance\n• **Avoid disputes** - Reduce likelihood of disagreements\n\n**How to Apply:**\n\n1. **Apply in prescribed form** - To relevant tax authority\n2. **Include required information** - Transaction details, financial implications\n3. **Tax authority responds** - Within **21 days** or gives reasons\n4. **Ruling issued** - In prescribed form\n\n**Application Must Include:**\n\n• **Taxpayer details** - Name, TIN, address, contact\n• **Transaction description** - Complete details\n• **Financial implications** - Tax impact\n• **Statutory provisions** - Legal basis\n• **Reasons** - Why ruling should be granted\n• **Court status** - Whether matter is before court\n\n**When Ruling is Valid:**\n\n• **Limited to applicant** - Only applies to you\n• **Specific transaction** - Only for that transaction\n• **Based on facts** - Facts must match actual transaction\n• **No fraud** - Must be truthful\n\n**When Ruling is Rejected:**\n\n• **Foreign law** interpretation\n• **Before court** - Issue already in court\n• **Constitutional** matters\n• **Academic/hypothetical** questions\n• **Interferes** with ongoing audit\n\n**When Ruling Becomes Void:**\n\n• **Transaction differs** - Materially different from description\n• **Fraud** - Misrepresentation or non-disclosure\n• **Conditions not met** - Assumptions not satisfied\n• **Law changed** - Provision repealed or amended\n• **Court overturns** - Interpretation overturned\n\n**Important:**\n\n• **Free service** - No fees charged\n• **21-day response** - Tax authority must respond promptly\n• **Binding** - On tax authority if conditions met\n• **Can be withdrawn** - If fraudulently obtained\n\n**Note:** Advance rulings help reduce uncertainty and avoid disputes. Apply before completing complex transactions.",
