      answer: "**Office of the Tax Ombud - For Businesses:**\n\n**What is the Tax Ombud?**\n\nThe Tax Ombud is an independent office that protects taxpayer rights and resolves complaints about tax authorities.\n\n**For Your Business:**\n\n**You Can Complain About:**\n\n• Actions or decisions of tax authorities\n• Tax officials' conduct\n• Regulatory fees and charges\n• Customs duty matters\n• Administrative issues\n• Abuse of office or breach of procedure\n\n**Services Provided:**\n\n• **Independent review** of your complaint\n• **Mediation** or conciliation (informal, fair, cost-effective)\n• **Investigation** of complaints\n• **Recommendations** to tax authorities\n• **Legal proceedings** on your behalf (if needed)\n• **Information** about taxpayer rights\n\n**Complaint Process:**\n\n1. **Lodge complaint** (in writing or through platform)\n2. **Issue must be unresolved** by tax authority first\n3. **Office reviews** within 14 days\n4. **Investigation** conducted\n5. **Resolution** through mediation or recommendations\n6. **Follow-up** on implementation\n\n**Important:**\n\n• **Free service** - No fees charged ✅\n• Must try resolving with tax authority first\n• Cannot handle issues already in court\n• Cannot determine tax liability (only administrative/procedural issues)\n• Anonymous complaints not entertained\n\n**Note:** The Tax Ombud ensures fair treatment and protects your business rights as a taxpayer.",
