      question: "When does my business need to register for tax and VAT?",
      answer: "**Business Tax Registration:**\n\n**Tax Registration (TIN):**\n\n• **All companies** - Must register regardless of size\n• **Every taxable person** - Anyone carrying out economic activity\n• **Before filing** - Get TIN before first return\n• **5 working days** - Tax authority must issue TIN or give reasons\n\n**VAT Registration:**\n\n• **Turnover ≥ ₦100 million** - Must register and charge VAT\n• **Turnover < ₦100 million** - Exempt from VAT (small business)\n• **Voluntary registration** - Small businesses can opt-in\n• **Monthly returns** - If registered, file by 21st of following month\n\n**Notification Requirements:**\n\n**Within 30 days, notify tax authority of:**\n\n• **Change of address** - Business location\n• **Change of name** - Trading name\n• **Change of owners** - 5%+ shareholders or beneficial owners\n• **Business structure** - Partnership, trust details\n• **Cessation** - Permanent or temporary cessation\n\n**Penalties:**\n\n• **Non-registration:** ₦50,000 first month, ₦25,000 each subsequent month\n• **Failure to notify changes:** ₦100,000 first month, ₦5,000 each subsequent month\n\n**Important:**\n\n• **Register early** - Before starting operations\n• **One TIN per business** - Cannot have multiple TINs\n• **Update changes** - Notify tax authority promptly\n• **Keep records** - Proof of registration and changes\n\n**Note:** OTax helps you track registration requirements and deadlines for your business.",
