      question: "What are the filing deadlines for company tax returns?",
      answer: "**Company Tax Return Deadlines:**\n\n**Existing Companies (>18 months):**\n\n• **Within 6 months** after end of accounting year\n• **Audited financial statements** required\n• **Self-assessment form** must be completed\n• **Tax computation** schedules\n• **Evidence of payment** included\n\n**New Companies (<18 months):**\n\n• **Within 18 months** of incorporation OR\n• **Within 6 months** after first accounting period ends\n• **Whichever is earlier**\n\n**Companies Ceasing Operations:**\n\n• **Within 6 months** from date of cessation\n• **Final returns** for cessation year\n• **Any outstanding returns** must be filed\n\n**Small Company Returns:**\n\n• **Statement of accounts** attested by taxpayer (instead of audited)\n• **Same deadlines** apply\n• **Still must file** even if exempt from CIT\n\n**Non-Resident Companies:**\n\n• **Full audited financial statements**\n• **Nigerian operations** financial statements\n• **Attested by qualified accountant** in Nigeria\n• **Same deadlines** apply\n\n**Penalties for Late Filing:**\n\n• **First month:** ₦100,000\n• **Each subsequent month:** ₦50,000\n• **Continues** until return is filed\n\n**Important:**\n\n• **File even if exempt** - All companies must file\n• **Meet deadlines** - Avoid penalties\n• **Include all required documents** - Complete returns\n\n**Note:** OTax helps you track filing deadlines and ensures you file complete returns on time.",
