      question: "What are the penalties for failing to deduct or remit tax at source?",
      answer: "**Withholding Tax Obligations:**\n\n**What Must Be Deducted:**\n\n• **Dividends** - Paid to shareholders\n• **Interest** - On loans, bonds, securities\n• **Rent** - Paid to landlords\n• **Royalties** - For use of intellectual property\n• **Director's fees** - Paid to directors\n• **Entertainer/sports fees** - Payments to performers\n• **Consulting fees** - Professional services\n\n**Penalties:**\n\n**Failure to Deduct:**\n\n• **40%** of amount not deducted\n• **Administrative penalty** - Enforceable as tax debt\n\n**Failure to Remit:**\n\n• **Amount not remitted** - Must be paid\n• **10% per annum** administrative penalty\n• **Interest** - CBN Monetary Policy Rate\n• **Criminal conviction** - Up to 3 years imprisonment or fine\n\n**Remittance Deadline:**\n\n• **By 21st day** - Of month following deduction\n• **Strict deadline** - Late remittance attracts penalties\n\n**Monthly Returns:**\n\n• **File monthly returns** - Showing deductions and remittances\n• **In prescribed form** - As required by tax authority\n\n**Important:**\n\n• **Deduct correctly** - Use correct rates\n• **Remit on time** - By 21st of following month\n• **File returns** - Monthly returns required\n• **Keep records** - Proof of deductions and remittances\n\n**Note:** OTax helps you track withholding tax obligations and ensures timely remittances.",
