      answer: "**Virtual Assets Service Providers (VASP):**\n\n**What is a VASP?**\n\nA VASP provides services related to:\n• **Exchange** of virtual assets\n• **Trading** of virtual assets\n• **Custody** of virtual assets\n• **Management** of virtual assets\n\n**Registration Requirements:**\n\n• **Must register** - With relevant tax authority as VASP\n• **License required** - From Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC)\n• **Before commencement** - Must be licensed first\n\n**Tax Obligations:**\n\n**1. Monthly Returns:**\n\n• **By 21st** of following month\n• **Additional information** required:\n  - Description of virtual asset services\n  - Transaction dates\n  - Type and value of virtual assets\n  - Customer details (name, address, TIN, NIN)\n  - Counterparty details\n\n**2. Record Keeping:**\n\n• **Keep records** - All transactions\n• **Customer information** - KYC requirements\n• **Transaction history** - At least 7 years\n\n**3. Reporting Obligations:**\n\n• **Large transactions** - Report to NRS and NFIU\n• **Suspicious transactions** - Report within 48 hours\n• **Periodic reports** - Customer transactions to NRS\n• **SCUML Certificate** - Required for AML compliance\n\n**Taxable Transactions:**\n\n• **Sale/exchange** of virtual assets\n• **Mining/staking** income\n• **Airdrops/bounties** - Received as compensation\n• **Payment for goods/services** - Using virtual assets\n\n**Valuation:**\n\n• **Market price** - At time of transaction\n• **Recognized exchange** - Approved by tax authority\n\n**Penalties:**\n\n• **Non-compliance:** ₦10,000,000 first month\n• **Each subsequent month:** ₦1,000,000\n• **License suspension** - Or revocation by SEC\n\n**Important:**\n\n• **Register early** - Before starting operations\n• **Obtain SEC license** - Required for operation\n• **Comply with AML** - Anti-money laundering requirements\n• **Keep detailed records** - All transactions\n\n**Note:** Virtual assets are taxable. Ensure proper registration and compliance.",
